# A ball from a one-limb center and a radius, both from the program and both guarded (rule R3):
# ball_make_2 with the center guarded as well, here c0 = guard(c), and no k1 (milestone1.md,
# "Values that enter from the program").
kernel:        ball_make_1
input:         c
input:         r
output:        cw
output:        rw
ensures:       makes_ball cw rw from=c,r
min_precision: 1
source:        constructors (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   every output is selected after explicit tests of the center and the radius (e, f); makes_ball states what comes out

g   = guard(r)
c0  = guard(c)
e   = le(0, g)
a   = abs(c0)
f1  = lt(a, const inf)
f2  = lt(g, const inf)
f   = and(f1, f2)
k0  = select(f, c0, 0)
s   = select(f, g, const inf)
cw  = select(e, k0, const nan)
rw  = select(e, s, const nan)
